.TH FSZERO 1 "August 2026" "FSZero" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fszero \- standalone FSZero operator CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fszero
.I COMMAND
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
FSZero is the byte and filesystem authority for the Zero family. The standalone
CLI provides diagnostics, batch operations, store maintenance, recovery, and
machine-readable capability inspection. Model-facing orchestration belongs to
the ZeroKernel host.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Show command help.
.TP
.B doctor
Report root resolution, store health, and recovery configuration.
.TP
.B batch
Execute one standalone batch request.
.TP
.B store-gc
Inspect or run bounded recovery-store garbage collection.
.TP
.B telemetry
Inspect default-off local usage accounting.
.TP
.B zeroref-fixture
Verify portable blob-ref fixtures.
.TP
.B capabilities
Print machine-readable FSZero capability and ownership metadata.
.TP
.B layout
Report repository and durable-store layout.
.TP
.B robot-triage
Print a compact machine-readable health summary.
.TP
.B robot-docs
Render current standalone operator documentation.
.TP
.B completions
Generate shell completion output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success, 1 an operational failure, and 2 invalid arguments or
contract syntax.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FSZERO_ROOT
Standalone workspace root.
.TP
.B FSZERO_SHARED_STORE
Opt into a configured shared ZeroStack store.
.TP
.B ZEROSTACK_STORE_ROOT
Shared store root, honored only with explicit opt-in.
.TP
.B FSZERO_ALLOW_EPHEMERAL
Allow disposable in-memory recovery when the durable store cannot open.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cargo (1)
and the FSZero README and docs/architecture.md files.
